Package: meshcore
Title: One Verb Set for Lattice Meshes: Rasters and Discrete Global Grids
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Michael", "Sumner", email = "mdsumner@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Prototype for the mesh core (working name). A raster (GRID) and a
    discrete global grid (CELL) are both meshes whose vertex, edge and
    boundary tables are computed from cell ids, so no coincident vertices are
    ever merged. The same verbs work on both, and arrays join to either model
    through a keyed dimension (cell id). Vocabulary follows UGRID, xdggs,
    uxarray and OGC API DGGS; vertex and segment tables follow wkpool.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
